# Design Narrative
# Mechanic: Manifest Dread top-two choice, face-down projection, and mana-cost turn-face-up action.
# Forcing: Centaur Courser is only lethal after it is selected, manifested, and turned face up from 2/2 to 3/3.
# AI behavior: Human performs every meaningful action; Unnerving Grasp removes the AI's only blocker before combat.
# Failure modes:
#   WIN = choice, zone split, face-down state, turn-up action, and combat result all worked.
#   LOSE = one of those steps failed before exact-lethal combat completed.
#   TIMEOUT = the resolution choice or turn-face-up interaction did not complete.
# Card roles:
#   Unnerving Grasp — creates the Manifest Dread resolution and removes the blocker.
#   Centaur Courser — selected creature; 3 power makes turning face up mandatory for lethal.
#   Island — unselected top card that must move to the graveyard.
#   Fervor — lets the newly manifested creature attack this turn.
#   Grizzly Bears — blocks the lethal attack unless Unnerving Grasp resolves its first effect.
# Protocol path: Cast/SelectTargetsReq, SelectNReq 13125, Library zone split, FaceDown REASON=8, SpecialTurnFaceUp action.

[metadata]
Name:Manifest Dread Unnerving Grasp
Goal:Win
Turns:1
Difficulty:Medium
Description:Manifest Centaur Courser, turn it face up, and attack for exact lethal.

